# Sir Godfrey Gwilym travelling with the party (docs/voice/sir_godfrey_gwilym.md): short lines a guest says while walking with the party, shown and voiced
# like banter (story/banter.gd). The node's name says when it may play: quest_ on entering an area while their story is
# at that point (these come first), place_ on entering an area, fight_ after a won fight, idle_ now and then on the
# road. Each plays once per playthrough, only while Sir Godfrey is with the party. Every line here is unvoiced for now.

~ quest_beacon
if guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym and flag.argynvost_beacon_lit
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: The beacon's lit. I saw it from the road and forgot, for a moment, that I was dead. It was a lovely moment.
endif
-> END

~ quest_oath
if guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym and flag.godfrey_remembers
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: I remember the oath now. All of it. I keep saying it under my breath, in case it tries to leave again.
endif
-> END

~ place_argynvostholt
if guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym and region:argynvostholt
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: Mind the steps. I've said it to every visitor for a hundred years. Today I find I'm saying it to myself.
endif
-> END

~ place_castle
if guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym and region:castle_ravenloft
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: We rode up this hill once, the whole Order, in silver. I remember the horses. I can't remember the faces. That seems unfair to the faces.
endif
-> END

~ place_krezk
if guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym and region:krezk
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: We wintered in Krezk once, I think. Or it was another village. They had pears. I'm sure of the pears.
endif
-> END

~ fight_nothing
if guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: Well fought. I felt nothing, which is the trouble with being dead, but I'm told it went well.
endif
-> END

~ fight_ride
if guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: One more ride, I said. I think that counted. I'd like another.
endif
-> END

~ fight_word
if guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: Is anyone hurt? I had a word for the kind of hurt that wants a priest. I had it a moment ago.
endif
-> END

~ idle_gwenllian
if guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: My sister Gwenllian laughed like a goose. I can't remember her face, but I'd know that laugh in a crowd of a thousand.
endif
-> END

~ idle_list
if guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: I read my list every night. Tonight I'll add all of you. Your names, and what you loved. You'll have to tell me the second part.
endif
-> END

~ idle_mare
if guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: I had a grey mare. Lovely creature, terrible manners. If there's a field after this, I hope she's in it, kicking someone.
endif
-> END
